# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# **gcloud does NOT read `.dockerignore`.** It reads this file, and with no
# `.gcloudignore` present it uploads everything under `server/` - which on
# 2026-09-10 meant 35,149 files and 363.9 MiB, almost all of it
# `frontend/node_modules` (332 MB) and `.venv` (105 MB). Both are rebuilt inside
# the image (`npm ci` in the node stage, `pip install` in the python stage), so
# uploading them is pure waste and slows every deploy.
#
# Keep this in step with `.dockerignore`: that one governs `docker build`
# locally and in compose, this one governs Cloud Build. Two files, same intent,
# because two tools read different names.

.git
.gitignore

# Rebuilt by `pip install -r requirements.txt` in the image.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Rebuilt by `npm ci` in the node stage.
frontend/node_modules/

# Build outputs - the image produces its own.
frontend/dist/
static/app/
staticfiles/

# Never ship secrets or local state.
.env
*.sqlite3
media/

# Test noise.
.pytest_cache/
junit*.xml
